 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Sure. A complementary color is any hue on opposite side of the color wheel from a given primary color. For example, the complementary of yellow is purple. Complementary colors make each other stand out strongly. If you use yellow as the base color, purple will look much deeper and brighter against it. Definitely. Purple shadows on yellow make them stand out. You don' need to skip it completely, just use it sparingly. A few dark purple shadows can make a big difference.",
